Safety and cost
---------------
New sites are in file operations, syscall helper paths and administrative
ioctls. There are no new sites in interrupt filters, NMI/IPI paths, scheduler
internals, boot initialization, allocator internals, packet fast paths, or
DTrace itself. Objects remain referenced at use; state fields are observed
under their existing mutexes. The last-reference semaphore identity is emitted
before free; no field is read afterward. Probe expressions perform no state
changes, allocation, formatting, payload copies or unconditional timing.
SDT's inactive patchpoints are verified as NOPs, and no-hooks builds contain
none of the new definitions. Enabled probes still cost time and may be high
volume on busy descriptor/semaphore workloads; select profiles narrowly.

Profiles and installation
-------------------------
  kernel-sem-resources
  kernel-sem-waits
  kernel-sem-decisions
  kernel-counterfd-waits
  kernel-counterfd-io
  kernel-tunnel-controls

The existing bsdinstruments profile glob selects all six for installation to
/usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles in the base bsdinstruments package. The
catalog now has 381 entries. Pair profiles use per-pid/tid depth and timestamps,
aggregate latency in microseconds by errno, and clear completed state. Event
profiles count numeric outcomes/transitions without dereferencing pointers.
Start tracing before workload; event loss invalidates pairing. PID filters
select execution context, not the owner of an opaque kernel object.

Validation and reproduction
---------------------------
Artifacts: /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace-eleventh-validation
Prepared kernel: /usr/obj/usr/src/amd64.amd64/sys/GENERIC-NODEBUG
Maintained drivers: coverage-eleventh-{compile,variants,modules,check}.py.
Compilation uses all available CPUs (16 here) and treats warnings as errors.

  12 native kernel object builds: six sources, KDTRACE_HOOKS on/off.
   2 additional semaphore builds: MAC and COMPAT_FREEBSD32 off, hooks on/off.
   4 linked modules: sem, if_gif, if_gre and if_vxlan.
   1 prepared kernel link, with make-selected object/probe symbol verification.
  12 executable object checks: enabled definitions have real executable
     patchpoints with inactive NOP instructions; disabled definitions absent.
  12 offline profile compilations: each normal and PID/duration filtered;
     selectors/argument counts and installation selection checked separately.

No kernel/module was installed, loaded or booted. /dev/dtrace is unavailable;
no live probe firing, lock-stress, traffic, timing accuracy or hardware testing
is claimed. The running kernel cannot validate these newly compiled sites.
Coverage is native amd64 plus the stated option variations, not every kernel
configuration or architecture. The manifest hashes this source snapshot;
session.patch contains only this round's changes over preserved dirty-tree
baselines, checked in reverse against the current tree.
